{
  "topic": "The science of lightning",
  "language": "en",
  "format": "long",
  "category": "ciencia",
  "title": "Could You CONTROL LIGHTNING? The Science of Thunder Power ⚡",
  "hook": "Some movie heroes and gods throw lightning with a hammer or their bare hands. Could anyone really control lightning?",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_hook",
      "narration": "Some movie heroes and gods throw lightning with a hammer or their bare hands. Could anyone really control lightning?",
      "on_screen_text": "Control lightning?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "lightning?"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_heat",
      "narration": "Before trying, know your enemy: a lightning bolt is five times hotter than the surface of the Sun.",
      "on_screen_text": "Hotter than the Sun",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Sun"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_count",
      "narration": "I'm Leo, and today we'll see what lightning really is and how far humans have learned to guide it.",
      "on_screen_text": "Guiding lightning",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Guiding"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_cloud",
      "narration": "It all starts inside a thundercloud. Strong winds rise and make ice crystals collide with soft hail.",
      "on_screen_text": "Inside the storm",
      "highlight_words": [
        "storm"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "An electricity factory"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_charges",
      "narration": "Millions of collisions separate the charges: positive on top, negative at the bottom, and the ground charges the opposite way.",
      "on_screen_text": "Separated charges",
      "highlight_words": [
        "charges"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_charges",
      "narration": "It's like rubbing a balloon on your hair, but on a giant scale: the cloud charges up like a huge battery.",
      "on_screen_text": "Like a rubbed balloon",
      "highlight_words": [
        "balloon"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_cloud",
      "narration": "In Venezuela, over Lake Maracaibo, there are storms almost every night: the famous Catatumbo lightning.",
      "on_screen_text": "Catatumbo lightning",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Catatumbo"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_cloud",
      "narration": "Some thunderclouds tower more than ten kilometers high, taller than Mount Everest.",
      "on_screen_text": "Clouds taller than Everest",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Everest"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_leader",
      "narration": "When the charge difference gets huge, a channel of charged air steps down from the cloud, looking for the ground.",
      "on_screen_text": "It steps down",
      "highlight_words": [
        "steps"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "How it strikes"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_strike",
      "narration": "A spark rises from the ground to meet it. When they touch, the current rushes through all at once: that's the flash.",
      "on_screen_text": "The flash!",
      "highlight_words": [
        "flash!"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_heat",
      "narration": "That channel heats the air to about thirty thousand degrees Celsius in a fraction of a second.",
      "on_screen_text": "30,000 degrees",
      "highlight_words": [
        "30,000"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_heat",
      "narration": "When lightning hits sand, it can melt it into glass tubes called fulgurites.",
      "on_screen_text": "Glass made by lightning",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Glass"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_thunder",
      "narration": "The air expands so fast that it bursts like an explosion. That's thunder.",
      "on_screen_text": "That's thunder",
      "highlight_words": [
        "thunder"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_thunder",
      "narration": "Up close it sounds like a sharp crack; far away, like a long rumble, because sound arrives from different parts of the channel.",
      "on_screen_text": "Crack or rumble",
      "highlight_words": [
        "rumble"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_count",
      "narration": "Since light arrives before sound, count the seconds between flash and thunder: every three seconds is roughly one kilometer.",
      "on_screen_text": "3 seconds ≈ 1 km",
      "highlight_words": [
        "kilometer"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_tower",
      "narration": "Can we control it? Partly, yes. More than two hundred years ago, Benjamin Franklin invented the lightning rod.",
      "on_screen_text": "The lightning rod",
      "highlight_words": [
        "rod"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "Taming lightning"
    },
    {
      "id": "s17",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_tower",
      "narration": "A metal tip connected to the ground offers lightning a safe path, protecting whole buildings.",
      "on_screen_text": "A safe path",
      "highlight_words": [
        "safe"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s18",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_tower",
      "narration": "And yes, lightning can strike the same place twice: New York's Empire State Building gets about twenty strikes a year.",
      "on_screen_text": "Twice, and more",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Twice"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s19",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_tower",
      "narration": "Planes get struck too, but they're designed so the current flows around the outside without hurting passengers.",
      "on_screen_text": "Lightning-proof planes",
      "highlight_words": [
        "planes"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s20",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_strike",
      "narration": "The closest thing to throwing lightning: scientists launch small rockets trailing a wire into a storm, and lightning follows it down.",
      "on_screen_text": "Lightning on demand",
      "highlight_words": [
        "demand"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s21",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_leader",
      "narration": "That's how they study lightning up close and test protection for planes, power lines and buildings.",
      "on_screen_text": "Studying it up close",
      "highlight_words": [
        "close"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_leader",
      "narration": "That channel looks for the easiest path through the air, which is why lightning looks crooked and full of branches.",
      "on_screen_text": "Crooked and branching",
      "highlight_words": [
        "branches"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s23",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "aur_storm",
      "narration": "But storing a bolt's energy isn't practical: it lasts only an instant and strikes wherever it wants.",
      "on_screen_text": "Hard to catch",
      "highlight_words": [
        "catch"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s24",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "aur_storm",
      "narration": "Besides, almost all of its energy turns into light, heat and sound in a single instant.",
      "on_screen_text": "Light, heat and sound",
      "highlight_words": [
        "heat"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s25",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_hook",
      "narration": "Most important of all: if you can hear thunder, you're close enough to be struck by lightning.",
      "on_screen_text": "When thunder roars",
      "highlight_words": [
        "thunder"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "Stay safe"
    },
    {
      "id": "s26",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_hook",
      "narration": "Go into a building or a closed car, and stay away from lone trees, water and open spaces.",
      "on_screen_text": "Find shelter",
      "highlight_words": [
        "shelter"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_hook",
      "narration": "Every second, dozens of lightning bolts strike somewhere on the planet, day and night.",
      "on_screen_text": "Dozens per second",
      "highlight_words": [
        "second"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_count",
      "narration": "Wait about thirty minutes after the last thunder before going back outside.",
      "on_screen_text": "Wait 30 minutes",
      "highlight_words": [
        "30"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s29",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_strike",
      "narration": "So nobody throws lightning with their hands, but science has learned to guide it, study it and protect us from it.",
      "on_screen_text": "Science guides it",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Science"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_strike",
      "narration": "It all happens very fast: the flash lasts far less than a second, though it sometimes flickers several times.",
      "on_screen_text": "A flickering flash",
      "highlight_words": [
        "flickers"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s31",
      "role": "closing",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ray_outro",
      "narration": "Which other movie power should we analyze next? Tell me in the comments.",
      "on_screen_text": "Which power next?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "power"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    }
  ],
